fix(tool-market): the alignment gate reports its own id, not data

The first live judge_setup run printed two gates both labelled `data`: the timeframe
gate was returning id 'data' because the Gate union had no 'alignment' member, so the
verdict named the wrong rule and the reader could not tell the two apart.

Now the gate owns its id, and the verdict prefixes the deciding gate ('alignment: ...',
'three-piece: ...') so a reader knows which rule closed the door.

Also states his step-1 branches properly instead of folding them into one line: with
weekly < 20 and daily >= 20 the corpus permits SHORT-TERM ONLY (no held position), and
that depends on a holding period this tool is not told — so it reports the rule as
UNKNOWN rather than inventing a verdict on the caller's behalf.

Three new tests, including 'never emits two gates with the same id' — the defect that
only showed up when a real proposal ran through every gate at once.

35 test files, 555 tests.